The Nautilus DevOps team needs to create an AWS Kinesis data stream for real-time data processing. 
This stream will be used to ingest and process large volumes of streaming data, which will then be consumed by various applications for analytics and real-time decision-making.

The stream should be named datacenter-stream.

Use Terraform to create this Kinesis stream.

The Terraform working directory is /home/bob/terraform. Create the main.tf file (do not create a different .tf file) to accomplish this task.

Note:

Right-click under the EXPLORER section in VS Code and select Open in Integrated Terminal to launch the terminal.
Before submitting the task, ensure that terraform plan returns No changes. Your infrastructure matches the configuration.

SOLUTION
To create the Kinesis data stream datacenter-stream, here is your /home/bob/terraform/main.tf:

hcl
resource "aws_kinesis_stream" "datacenter_stream" {
  name = "datacenter-stream"

  tags = {
    Name = "datacenter-stream"
  }
}
💡 Key Details
Resource: aws_kinesis_stream creates a Kinesis data stream.

Name: Exactly datacenter-stream as required.

Shard Count: Not specified in the task, so it's omitted. Terraform will use the provider's default behavior. If your provider version requires shard_count, you can add shard_count = 1.

Region: Handled by your existing provider.tf (us-east-1), so no extra provider block is needed.

🚀 Execution Steps
bash
cd /home/bob/terraform
terraform init
terraform plan
terraform apply --auto-approve
✅ Ensure terraform plan Shows No Changes
After applying, run:

bash
terraform plan
It should return:

text
No changes. Your infrastructure matches the configuration.
🔍 Verify (optional)
bash
aws --endpoint-url=http://aws:4566 kinesis describe-stream --stream-name datacenter-stream
You should see the stream with status ACTIVE.

⚠️ If shard_count Is Required
Some provider versions require shard_count to be explicitly set. If terraform apply fails with a missing argument error, update the resource to:

hcl
resource "aws_kinesis_stream" "datacenter_stream" {
  name        = "datacenter-stream"
  shard_count = 1

  tags = {
    Name = "datacenter-stream"
  }
}
Then run terraform apply --auto-approve again.

Error: shard_count must be at least 1 when stream_mode is PROVISIONED
│ 
│   with aws_kinesis_stream.datacenter_stream,
│   on main.tf line 1, in resource "aws_kinesis_stream" "datacenter_stream":
│    1: resource "aws_kinesis_stream" "datacenter_stream" {
The error confirms that shard_count is required when the stream mode defaults to PROVISIONED. Add shard_count = 1 to fix it. Here is the updated /home/bob/terraform/main.tf:

hcl
resource "aws_kinesis_stream" "devops_stream" {
  name        = "devops-stream"
  shard_count = 1
}
💡 Why This Fixes It
The AWS provider defaults stream_mode to PROVISIONED.

In PROVISIONED mode, shard_count is a required argument and must be at least 1.

Setting shard_count = 1 satisfies the requirement.

